<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      So the wallet's coin selection can be tested as the pure function it is. It decides which VTXOs
      carry a player's heroes into a spend, and that is worth asserting directly rather than only
      through a live arkd. Internal rather than public because nothing outside the wallet should call it.
    -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="ArkadeHeroes.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\ArkadeHeroes.Core\ArkadeHeroes.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\external\dotnet-sdk\NArk\NArk.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\external\dotnet-sdk\NArk.Arkade\NArk.Arkade.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\external\dotnet-sdk\NArk.Storage.EfCore\NArk.Storage.EfCore.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite" Version="10.0.9" />
    <!--
      CVE-2025-6965 (GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q, CVSS 7.2): SQLite before 3.50.2 lets the number of aggregate
      terms exceed the columns available, corrupting memory. EF Core pulls the native library through
      SQLitePCLRaw, and EF 10.0.10 — the newest — STILL pins bundle_e_sqlite3/core 2.1.11, whose bundled
      SQLite is affected. So there is no supported fix to wait for at the EF level.

      lib.e_sqlite3 is a PURE NATIVE-ASSET package (its nuspec declares no dependencies at all — just
      "builds of the native SQLite code for various platforms"), while the managed P/Invoke surface lives
      in SQLitePCLRaw.core. Naming it here therefore swaps ONLY the native binary for a patched build and
      leaves the managed stack on the 2.1.11 that EF expects. The alternative — bundle_e_sqlite3 3.0.5 — is
      a major bump that restructures the graph and would leave core at 2.1.11 anyway, i.e. a mixed 2.1/3.0
      provider stack under an EF pinned to 2.1.11. Same benefit, worse risk.

      Version chosen for the WASM side too, deliberately: this package version scheme now tracks the
      bundled SQLite, and 3.50.3 ships runtimes/browser-wasm/nativeassets/net9.0/e_sqlite3.a — the exact
      asset our net10.0 browser build already resolves from 2.1.11 (neither version ships a net10.0 one),
      so the in-browser wallet's storage swaps like-for-like. Keep this in step with ArkadeHeroes.Web.
      Drop this line once EF's own SQLitePCLRaw floor reaches a patched SQLite.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3" Version="3.50.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
